<!-- STRUCTURE GUIDE -->
<section class="oop-section">
    <div class="oop-section-header">
        <div class="oop-section-icon">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i>
        </div>
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Structure Guide</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p class="section-intro">Click each section to expand. Add new methods to your existing classes.</p>
    
    <!-- 1. consume in Inventory -->
    <details class="skeleton-block" open>
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">1</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">consume (in Inventory)</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-line code">METHOD consume(item_id) → boolean:</div>
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <strong>Purpose:</strong> Remove a consumable item from inventory<br><br>
                Works the same as <code>remove()</code> — the engine decides what's consumable.
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- 2. use_item setup -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">2</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">use_item Setup (in Player)</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-line code">METHOD use_item(item_id, target) → string:</div>
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                <strong>First:</strong> Check if item is in inventory<br>
                If not found, return: <code>"You don't have 'item_id'."</code>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- 3. Item handling -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">3</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">use_item Logic</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                Use conditional logic to handle each item type:
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>keycard</strong> → return unlock message</li>
                    <li><strong>crowbar</strong> → return pry open message</li>
                    <li><strong>med_patch</strong> → call heal(20), consume item, return heal message</li>
                    <li><strong>torch</strong> → return illuminate message</li>
                    <li><strong>other</strong> → return "not sure how to use" message</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
    
    <!-- 4. Method chaining -->
    <details class="skeleton-block">
        <summary class="skeleton-summary">
            <span class="skeleton-step">4</span>
            <span class="skeleton-title">Method Chaining Example</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down skeleton-chevron"></i>
        </summary>
        <div class="skeleton-content">
            <div class="skeleton-desc">
                For med_patch, your code should:
                <ol>
                    <li>Call <code>heal(20)</code> to increase health</li>
                    <li>Call <code>inventory.consume("med_patch")</code> to remove it</li>
                    <li>Return a message like "You apply the med patch. +20 HP"</li>
                </ol>
                This is <strong>method integration</strong> — use_item calls heal and consume.
            </div>
        </div>
    </details>
</section>

